  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Blueprint Datasheet",
    "overview": "Skyfall's interface reads like an engineering drawing that has been typeset for the screen. Every surface is flat white or near-white paper, divided by 1px hairlines into cells, panels and figures. Labels are set in a monospace face, in caps, often prefixed with a slash, a square or angle brackets, the way a datasheet annotates a part. Headlines are enormous, tightly tracked and set in capitalised title case with line-heights below 1, so the words stack like a stencil on a drawing sheet. One blue carries every signal: the current nav tab, the focus ring, the selection highlight, the active bar in a chart, the hover state of a link. Nothing else is coloured except the seven muted \"pixel tones\" reserved for the 10×10 pixel icons.\n\nThe system is dense but calm. Space comes from generous section padding (64–112px) and from leaving cells of the grid empty, not from soft shadows or rounded containers. Depth is drawn, never cast: corner brackets, corner dots, dotted fields and grid fields mark where a figure sits. Motion follows the same logic as the layout, with lines of type rising out of masks, labels scrambling into place, bars growing from zero, counters counting up, and a blue panel sliding across a button on hover. Everything eases out on an expo curve and nothing bounces.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One accent (Skyfall Blue #3e57da) on an otherwise achromatic palette; a lighter lift (#6f83f0) replaces it on dark grounds.",
      "Zero border radius anywhere. Squares, brackets and hairlines are the only decoration.",
      "Geist for reading, Geist Mono for every label, button, meta line and tag. Mono is always small and usually uppercase.",
      "Hairline grids (#e0e0e0 on paper, #474747 on night) built from shared borders, so cells never double up.",
      "Five grounds: paper, studio, night (grid), ink and blue. Sections switch ground rather than adding cards.",
      "Motion is scroll-driven, masked and expo-eased; reduced-motion users get the same content with no animation."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Blue Rule",
        "body": "Skyfall Blue is the only saturated colour in the UI. If a second accent seems necessary, the answer is a hairline, a mono label or more white space.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lift Rule",
        "body": "On ink or night grounds, blue text and hover states use Blue Lift (#6f83f0), never the base blue, which fails contrast on #1a1a1a.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tone Quarantine Rule",
        "body": "Pixel tones live only inside pixel icons.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Annotation Rule",
        "body": "Anything that labels, counts, dates or tags is set in Geist Mono at 15px or smaller. Mono never carries a sentence of body copy.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sub-One Rule",
        "body": "Display and headline line-heights sit below 1.0 (0.85–0.95). Titles and body return to 1.15–1.65.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Medium Rule",
        "body": "Headlines are weight 500. Emphasis in prose is 600. 700 is not used.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Never add box-shadow. If something needs lifting, give it a 1px ink border, a title bar or a field behind it.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Draw-It Rule",
        "body": "Depth is implied by brackets, dots and rules, the way a drawing annotates a part.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep Skyfall Blue (#3e57da) to state and signal: current tab, hover, focus, selection, the active bar, dates, the / prefix.",
      "Do build groups as shared-border hairline grids (border-t border-l on the list, border-r border-b on cells).",
      "Do set every label, tag, meta line and button in Geist Mono, 11–15px, uppercase, with -0.02em tracking (or +0.05em at 11px).",
      "Do set headlines at weight 500 with -0.045em tracking and line-height under 1, and capitalise them.",
      "Do switch section grounds (paper → studio → night → blue) to create rhythm.",
      "Do frame figures with a left ink rule, corner brackets, corner dots or a dotted field.",
      "Do ease everything out on the expo curve and gate reveals on scroll position.",
      "Do keep touch targets at 44px and focus rings at 2px blue with 2px offset."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add border radius to anything.",
      "Don't add box shadows, gradients on surfaces or glassmorphism; the dialog backdrop blur is the single exception.",
      "Don't introduce a second accent colour or use pixel tones outside pixel icons.",
      "Don't use the base blue for text on ink or night grounds; use Blue Lift.",
      "Don't set body copy in mono or labels in Geist.",
      "Don't use weights above 600, or light weights below 400.",
      "Don't replace hairlines with spacing-only separation inside grids; the lines are the structure.",
      "Don't bounce, overshoot or spring; motion decelerates and stops."
    ]
  }
}